# Copy to .env and fill in. A TTS provider (ElevenLabs, Cartesia, HeyGen — or Drama 3 on Modal's
# free monthly credit) is the ONLY paid API
# the math and technical pipeline needs — every LLM step runs as a Claude Code subagent under your Claude
# subscription. The humanities (folio) pipeline adds two image keys: see the
# section at the bottom.

# --- Narration: choose ONE TTS provider and fill in its key + voice -----------------------
TTS_PROVIDER=elevenlabs              # elevenlabs | cartesia | heygen | drama3

# ElevenLabs — key needs text_to_speech; any voice ID, including a cloned voice.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=
#ELEVENLABS_TTS_MODEL=eleven_multilingual_v2  # eleven_turbo_v2_5 = half the credits

# Cartesia — e.g. a Pro Voice Clone.
#CARTESIA_API_KEY=sk_car_...
#CARTESIA_VOICE_ID=...
#CARTESIA_TTS_MODEL=sonic-3.6        # pin a dated snapshot for reproducible fixes

# HeyGen
#HEYGEN_API_KEY=...
#HEYGEN_VOICE_ID=...
#HEYGEN_EXPRESSIVENESS=0.5           # instant voices only, 0-1

# Drama 3 (open weights on a Modal GPU; US$30/month free credit covers hundreds of videos).
# No key here: `pip install modal && modal setup` stores the token in ~/.modal.toml, then
# `python scripts/drama3_modal.py download` once. The voice = 1-3 clips ref_N.wav + ref_N.txt.
#DRAMA3_REFS_DIR=inputs/voice/drama3_refs
#DRAMA3_TAGS=1                       # opt-in: inline delivery tags (<emphasis>, <slow>, [pause]) per script
#DRAMA3_STYLE=[a calm, engaged lecturer working through the algebra at the board]   # optional style prefix; off by default

# No pronunciation dictionary: narration is voiced verbatim, and tokens voices misread are
# respelled from the alias library (scripts/utils/tts_aliases.py), so any provider works.

# --- Transcription (optional) -------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed to transcribe an audio/video file, or a YouTube video without captions:
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY above with speech_to_text enabled (ElevenLabs Scribe, pay as you go),
# whichever TTS provider you chose. Without it, local files fall back to local Whisper.
#ELEVENLABS_STT_MODEL=scribe_v2      # Scribe transcription model

# Optional overrides (defaults shown)
#MANIM_RENDER_JOBS=2                 # parallel Manim frame renders
#MANIM_RENDER_TIMEOUT=1800           # seconds per frame render (raise for dense 4K frames)
#SUBTITLE_DRIFT_TOLERANCE=0.5        # seconds; raise to ~1.0 for very long videos
#SKIP_NARRATION_CHECK=               # set to 1 only to bypass a confirmed false positive

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Humanities pipeline (--folio) only — not needed for math/technical videos.
# Images: roughly US$10-12 per 20-minute episode (4K plates).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OpenAI Images API — engraved plates, portraits, objects and then-states. Requires
# access to gpt-image-2.5 (API id gpt-image-2.5-sunburst); there is no fallback model.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Google Gemini API (aistudio.google.com/apikey) — grounded maps (Gemini 3 Pro Image
# + Google Search).
# Optional motion plates (scripts/folio_motion.py, off by default) also use this key for
# Gemini Omni Flash (~US$1.10 per 10 s clip).
GOOGLE_CLOUD_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides (defaults shown)
#REMOTION_RENDER_TIMEOUT=1800        # seconds per scene render
